Assembler Version 09
====================
Assembled by: version 08 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 08, plus section directives, command-line arguments,
parameterized hash table module, and modular source organization:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n and \\ escapes
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment (including label refs)
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch labels (auto-detected via instruction flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection
- .include directive for including external files
- .zeropage section directive (new)
- .code section directive (new)
- Command-line arguments: <assembler> <input> <output> (new)

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switches to zero page section (new)
- .code - switches back to code section (new)

Instruction set: same as version 08, plus:
- ASLZ (ASL zero-page)

Error handling: same errors as version 08 (errors 1-E), plus:
- Usage error (error D): wrong number of command-line arguments

New in this version (relative to version 08):
- .zeropage and .code section directives: allows defining zero page variables
  separately from code, with automatic PC save/restore between sections
- IN_ZEROPAGE flag: suppresses code output during zero page section
- PC_SAVEL/PC_SAVEH: saves/restores program counter when switching sections
- Command-line arguments for input and output files: the assembler no longer
  reads from stdin; instead it takes input and output filenames as arguments
  via argc ($F01B) and argv ($F01E)
- Usage error message when wrong number of arguments provided
- Parameterized hash table module: common.asm extracted for shared code
  between asm.asm and instgen.asm
- ASLZ instruction added to instruction table
- First version using .include in its own source code (environment.asm,
  common.asm, out/inst.asm.out)
- Output via file handle: openout ($F021) and write ($F024) replace stdout

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Non-standard mnemonic syntax (LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, BITZ, INCZ, DECZ, etc.)
- DATA pseudo-instruction
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments (label = value)
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC for vectors)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Labels as absolute 2-byte operands
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message (BRK $xx "message" $00)
- .include directive (environment.asm, common.asm, out/inst.asm.out)
- Zero page variables via explicit = assignments (TEMP = $00, etc.)
- File I/O: open, close, read, openout, write
- File stack operations (push/pop) for .include handling
- Command-line arg access: argc, argv

New syntax used in source (relative to version 08):
- .include directive (first version to use .include in its own source,
  including environment.asm, common.asm, and out/inst.asm.out)

Other source changes:
- Source split into modules: asm.asm, common.asm, environment.asm, instgen.asm
- Command-line argument handling via argc/argv in start routine
- Output file opened via openout and argv (replaces stdout-only output)
- IN_ZEROPAGE flag and PC save/restore for section directive handling
- inst.asm.out now included via .include instead of prepended
